+/* GFX803 VA-recycling workaround: a freed VA is withheld from the aperture
+ * free-list until FMM_REUSE_QUEUE_MAX further frees have occurred, so a hot
+ * address is never handed straight back to the next same-size malloc. The
+ * parked object keeps its BOs and its VA reservation for the whole window.
+ * When the window expires the BO is freed during a later FREE call -- i.e.
+ * while the GPU is busy, which is the measured ingredient that clears the
+ * stale gfx803 memory-system state (a teardown at a GPU-quiescent point
+ * leaves 5-7 of 52 reduction-harness shapes wrong, the busy-time teardown
+ * leaves 0). Length-bounded (not alloc-counted) so it is O(1) per op and
+ * self-limiting for every aperture regardless of which alloc paths fire --
+ * an alloc-counted delay can grow unboundedly on apertures whose alloc path
+ * doesn't bump the counter. A byte cap bounds the extra VRAM held by parked
+ * BOs (4GB-class caps break real workloads with HIPBLAS_STATUS_ALLOC_FAILED).
+ */
+#define FMM_REUSE_QUEUE_MAX 256
+#define FMM_REUSE_BYTES_MAX (1ULL << 30)
+
